Spec: Bounded direct-first connection planning

Purpose:
  Select one fully authenticated business transport within an application's original opening budget.

Owns:
  ./ConnectionPlanner.java

Must:
  Include prior authorization/preparation time by accepting the original monotonic admission timestamp; never reset total or direct-wait budgets between attempts.
  Prefer direct within its configured window, use relay only when explicitly allowed, and spend the total budget on direct when relay is forbidden.
  Treat authentication, identity, unsupported capability, resource exhaustion and clock failures as terminal rather than bypassing them through another path.
  Keep partial attempts cancelable, close late results, transfer exactly one winning result and never replay application bytes or migrate an already returned stream.
  Use separate host-bounded direct/relay executors; no new threads or implicit retry loops belong to the planner.
  Return fixed path, fallback reason and setup duration separately from later actual business-byte counters.
  Reject unsupported prewarm and relay-byte-budget features before opening a transport.
